cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CACE-Bench: A Synthetic Agentic Evaluation Benchmark for LLM Credit-Pipeline Agents"
message: "If you use CACE-Bench, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Akhtyamov"
    given-names: "Ravil"
    affiliation: "Digital Economy Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rav11l/cace-bench"
url: "https://digitaleconomylab.org"
abstract: >-
  Compliance-Aware Credit-agent Evaluation (CACE-Bench): a fully synthetic,
  reproducible benchmark and generator for evaluating and auto-evolving
  LLM-agent credit pipelines under auditability constraints. Cases are drawn
  per country and each source class is resolved against a provider registry, so
  the benchmark measures what a pipeline does when the data it needs is not
  obtainable — not only whether it reasons correctly when everything is present.
  Reports silent-decision rate, provenance completeness, over-escalation rate,
  hallucination rate, recovery rate, compliance false-positive rate and
  step-level correctness, with 95% Wilson intervals, on 23,000 synthetic cases.
